{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.HookLengthFormula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HookLengthFormula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookGNW","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.ColLenRowLensBridge","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.numStandardYoungTableaux_mul_hookLengthProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.numStandardYoungTableaux_mul_hookLengthProduct","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HookLengthFormula.lean#L158-L185","doc":"**The hook-length formula (target)**: for every Young diagram `μ` with\n`n = |μ|` cells, the number of standard Young tableaux times the hook-length\nproduct equals `n!`:\n\n  `#SYT(μ) · ∏_{c ∈ μ} hook(c) = n!`.\n\nEquivalently `#SYT(μ) = n! / ∏ hook(c)`. This is the closed form that pins the\nper-shape counts (e.g. the hook `(2,1)`: hooks `3·1·1 = 3`, so\n`#SYT = 3!/3 = 2`, matching `SytSmallShapeCounts.card_SYT_mu21`).\n\nStated as the infra target; the proof (RSK, or the\nFrame–Robinson–Thrall / Novelli–Pak–Stoyanovskii probabilistic bijection) is\nthe tracked next step — a Mathlib-upstream-scale contribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.hookLengthProduct_eq_prodHooks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.hookLengthProduct_eq_prodHooks","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HookLengthFormula.lean#L135-L156","doc":"**The geometric↔list hook bridge** `∏_{c∈μ} hook(c) = prodHooks (rowLens μ)` (sorry-free).\nReindexes the cell product by rows (`cells_biUnion'`) and columns (`row_prod`), converts the\ncorpus list `prodHooks` product to a `Finset` product (`list_prod_map_range`), and identifies\nthe per-cell hook `(rowLen i − j) + (colLen j − i) − 1` (`hookLength_eq_of_mem` +\n`ColLenRowLensBridge.colLen_rowLens`) with the corpus list term. Together with the proved\nlist-form HLF (`QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_mul_prodHooks`) this fully discharges the\ngeometric Frame–Robinson–Thrall HLF below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:YoungDiagram.hookLengthProduct_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"YoungDiagram.hookLengthProduct_pos","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HookLengthFormula.lean#L82-L86","doc":"The hook-length product is positive (a product of positive hook lengths). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:YoungDiagram.hookLengthProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"YoungDiagram.hookLengthProduct","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HookLengthFormula.lean#L79-L80","doc":"**The hook-length product** `∏_{c ∈ μ} hook(c)` — the denominator of the HLF. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:YoungDiagram.hookLength_eq_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"YoungDiagram.hookLength_eq_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HookLengthFormula.lean#L68-L77","doc":"On a **cell** `(i, j) ∈ μ`, the hook length is the closed form\n`(rowLen i − j) + (colLen j − i) − 1`. On a cell `j < rowLen i` and\n`i < colLen j`, so arm `= rowLen i − j − 1` and leg `= colLen j − i − 1`\nare the honest right/below counts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:YoungDiagram.hookLength_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"YoungDiagram.hookLength_pos","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HookLengthFormula.lean#L65-L66","doc":"Hook lengths are always positive (the `+ 1` counts the cell itself). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:YoungDiagram.hookLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"YoungDiagram.hookLength","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HookLengthFormula.lean#L62-L63","doc":"**Hook length** of cell `(i, j)`: arm + leg + 1 (the cell, its arm, and its leg). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:YoungDiagram.legLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"YoungDiagram.legLength","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HookLengthFormula.lean#L58-L60","doc":"**Leg length** of cell `(i, j)`: the number of cells strictly below it in\ncolumn `j` (`colLen j − i − 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:YoungDiagram.armLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"YoungDiagram.armLength","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HookLengthFormula.lean#L54-L56","doc":"**Arm length** of cell `(i, j)`: the number of cells strictly to its right in\nrow `i` (`rowLen i − j − 1`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}